                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e326b150-0187-4a51-b6d5-8576d6768018",
                        "source_entry_id": "58e1da06-0fea-3481-b291-9d1b37c56911",
                        "target_lang_word": "Wasserpfeife",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Wasserpfeife",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b20dedc-67bf-302a-a266-6b85960f6674",
                                        "entry_id": "b356a3f6-f90a-3763-a9cf-e95e989e8864",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rauchgerät, bei dem die Rauchluft durch einen Wasserbehälter gezogen wird, bevor man ihn einatmet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b21d285-ccd3-4aee-a980-ba00ca60a410",
                                                "sense_id": "1b20dedc-67bf-302a-a266-6b85960f6674",
                                                "text": "Wasserpfeife zu rauchen ist etwas sehr geselliges und wird auch bei uns in Europa immer beliebter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d52bb013-0f14-4e5c-83a9-db605d6f01b0",
                                                "sense_id": "1b20dedc-67bf-302a-a266-6b85960f6674",
                                                "text": "„Ich hatte mir eine Wasserpfeife auf der Galata-Brücke verdient.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2939c667-0423-46a0-bfa9-711ac03b875c",
                                                "sense_id": "1b20dedc-67bf-302a-a266-6b85960f6674",
                                                "text": "„Vor dem Hotel Abdulla – auf dem Trottoir – saßen Männer im Halbkreis, rauchten Wasserpfeifen und tranken Türkischen aus kleinen, runden Tassen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf9f42e2-03d3-41a3-9a1d-0ef537f5d427",
                                                "sense_id": "1b20dedc-67bf-302a-a266-6b85960f6674",
                                                "text": "„Gegen Abend wurde es noch lebhafter in den kleinen Städtchen entlang meiner Route, die Straßencafés waren voller Menschen, die aus kleinen Tässchen Tee oder Kaffee tranken, Wasserpfeifen rauchten und plauderten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f579acf-5bf0-4e45-b5c7-3645b9141bba",
                                                "sense_id": "1b20dedc-67bf-302a-a266-6b85960f6674",
                                                "text": "„So nannten die Leute damals die Wasserpfeifen Narjiledes.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2254f9ce-6b11-4417-ae47-4af8544532b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "58e1da06-0fea-3481-b291-9d1b37c56911",
                        "target_lang_word": "hookah",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hookah",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cdd17230-6f1c-3978-81d5-d5767e09066f",
                                        "entry_id": "6da7803c-6dfc-3c6a-a8a9-66e1a27c54e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pipe with a long flexible tube that draws the smoke through water, traditionally used for smoking tobacco, which is often flavored."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a73418ca-92ae-42d1-8a9d-6217cc874cab",
                                                "sense_id": "cdd17230-6f1c-3978-81d5-d5767e09066f",
                                                "text": "In India, the lower orders use a hookah or hubble bubble, which is made of a cocoa-nut shell well cleaned out, having a hole through the soft eye of the shell, and another on the opposite side, a little lower down, the first of which is used for the chauffoir, and the other to suck or draw the smoke from."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f91f620-da16-4346-bed8-7e8bd1880ced",
                                                "sense_id": "cdd17230-6f1c-3978-81d5-d5767e09066f",
                                                "text": "Our new acquaintance very deliberately coiled up the tube of his hookah, and produced from behind a curtain a very long befrogged topcoat with Astrakhan collar and cuffs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a1af3a-f788-4943-a56c-080529e0b19a",
                                                "sense_id": "cdd17230-6f1c-3978-81d5-d5767e09066f",
                                                "text": "The lounge was furnished in old English oak and big Knole settees. There were rugs from Tabriz and Kerman on the highly polished floor. […] A table lamp was fashioned from a silver Egyptian hookah."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d83978a-d26c-4d75-94e2-2d681d10b556",
                                                "sense_id": "cdd17230-6f1c-3978-81d5-d5767e09066f",
                                                "text": "When Uncle Jack caught me, he kept me laughing about a preacher who hated going to church so much that every day he stood at his gate in his dressing-gown, smoking a hookah and delivering five-minute sermons to any passers-by who desired spiritual comfort."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8525a3b0-75e2-3de6-aec4-6900c6b74353",
                                        "entry_id": "6da7803c-6dfc-3c6a-a8a9-66e1a27c54e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tankless surface air compressor pump and umbilical piping system that supplies air to a diving mask."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "68b56cab-881c-45a1-a586-32678ca47d81",
                        "source_entry_id": "58e1da06-0fea-3481-b291-9d1b37c56911",
                        "target_lang_word": "narguilé",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "narguilé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df13d2fc-a4f0-3072-a7a1-ca09db393dfd",
                                        "entry_id": "802de2b5-efcb-35b6-aa1f-0cb88cf8bf24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pipe formée d’un fourneau, où brûle le tabac, et d’un long tuyau qui traverse un vase rempli d’eau parfumée, en usage en Turquie, en Perse et au Moyen-Orient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4add8e8b-9bb7-45da-9564-eb6998db0345",
                                                "sense_id": "df13d2fc-a4f0-3072-a7a1-ca09db393dfd",
                                                "text": "Ali, silencieux et attentif, apporta le tabac et les narguilés, servit le café et disparut."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d208c696-af7e-42c4-8f3d-d94e875b5676",
                                                "sense_id": "df13d2fc-a4f0-3072-a7a1-ca09db393dfd",
                                                "text": "Le cheikh n’était plus à sa place. Chose curieuse, le bout doré de son narguilé traînait par terre. D’ordinaire, quand il se levait, il enroulait le tuyau autour du foyer, d’une geste machinal, et retirait le bout pour le garder propre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9503a90f-b5e8-3ae9-bc3d-ad691fa82ec2",
                                        "entry_id": "802de2b5-efcb-35b6-aa1f-0cb88cf8bf24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tuyau qui fournit l’air au scaphandrier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6cd5cddf-f918-45f6-9747-9f85d508d595",
                        "source_entry_id": "58e1da06-0fea-3481-b291-9d1b37c56911",
                        "target_lang_word": "pipe à eau",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pipe à eau",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ae1db76-43fa-3c23-a813-600387c62089",
                                        "entry_id": "61b2df0e-2ab0-365d-92e5-08e3b031baff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pipe contenant de l’eau, permettant de générer et refroidir une grande quantité de fumée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9acb923-d302-4ae0-90d5-8f15b3345854",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae1db76-43fa-3c23-a813-600387c62089",
                                                "text": "Quand les voyageurs – Mokkhi devant, Ouroz sur Jehol au milieu et Zéré à l’arrière – eurent pris le chemin de Bamyian, le patron de la tchaïkhana revint s’accroupir près du narghilé et fuma. Ses amis attendaient leur tour et les anciens esclaves regardaient en silence la buée grise monter de la pipe à eau vers les feuilles desséchées de l’auvent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "506a3738-b1c4-4dbe-b9c9-ff8d7e59f012",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae1db76-43fa-3c23-a813-600387c62089",
                                                "text": "De forme variable selon les lieux, la pipe à eau orientale change aussi de nom : de kaliân en Perse à houka en Inde, elle perpétue une tradition dont l’origine n’est pas encore éclaircie, mais réclamerait une recherche scientifique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12094ed5-c896-4647-9e7e-a66b62f65a05",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae1db76-43fa-3c23-a813-600387c62089",
                                                "text": "Dans un pays [la Perse] où chaque homme, chaque femme et bon nombre d’enfants s’adonnent au plaisir de la cigarette ou de la pipe à eau, ce commerce était des plus fructueux."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2036bedb-7bc4-45f8-83cf-35df1ce247b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "58e1da06-0fea-3481-b291-9d1b37c56911",
